// SHP - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

// SHP: an ESRI shapefile. The header is one hundred bytes and
// mixes byte orders: the file code and the file length are big
// endian, everything after them is little endian.
//
// There is no greeting in this file, because there is nowhere in
// the format to put one. The five unused header bytes are
// specified as zero, the bounding box holds four doubles, and the
// Null Shape record that follows is four bytes of shape type. A
// `Hello World!` in any of them would be a file no reader accepts,
// so this one is a correct header with nothing to say.
//
// File code 9994, version 1000, shape type 0, and the length in
// 16-bit words that the format -- not the byte count.
//
// shp: 108 bytes, dumped sixteen at a time.
//
// The bytes below are not hand-written. They are built from the
// format's own field widths by scripts/build_object_formats.py, and
// scripts/verify_encodings.py reads the fields back by name -- the
// magic number, the lengths, the offsets. A hex dump written from
// memory is wrong in one byte and looks exactly like a correct one.
//

// 00 00 27 0A 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 36 00 00 00 |..'.........6...|   <- 0000
// 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 E8 03 00 00 00 00 00 |................|   <- 0010
// 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 |................|   <- 0020
// 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 |................|   <- 0030
// 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 |................|   <- 0040
// 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 |................|   <- 0050
// 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00             |............|   <- 0060
